body:
> That didn't work, did you mean "both `ignore-windows` and `needs-symlink`"?

As far as I can tell, the error is unrelated to whether the symlink works or not. This simply fails because we can't find `libc`:

```rs
use run_make_support::{create_symlink, fs_wrapper, rustc, path};

fn main() {
    let input = r#"
    #![feature(rustc_private)]
    extern crate libc;
    fn main() {}
    "#;
    rustc().stdin(&input).input("-").run();
}
```

@bors r-
https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/129254#issuecomment-2295414459
https://github.com/rust-lang-ci/rust/actions/runs/10443963448/job/28917967814#step:25:3430

This seems to have nothing to do with the test? Not to mention that it passed a bunch of try-jobs before, including MSVC.

Let's see if it's spurious.

@bors try

see also this note from the docs:
```
/// # Differences from `ExitStatus`
///
/// `ExitCode` is intended for terminating the currently running process, via
/// the `Termination` trait, in contrast to [`ExitStatus`], which represents the
/// termination of a child process. These APIs are separate due to platform
/// compatibility differences and their expected usage; it is not generally
/// possible to exactly reproduce an `ExitStatus` from a child for the current
/// process after the fact.
```

